# Prisma and MySQL

Provider is `mysql`. Prisma is 5.18 with `prismaSchemaFolder`. Auth models stay in `prisma/schema/auth.prisma`. Content models stay beside `Article`.

```prisma
exampleId String @id @db.Char(40)
```

- Generate with `yarn prisma migrate dev --name <name> --create-only`, then read the SQL.
- On a populated table, add a required column as nullable, backfill every row, then set `NOT NULL` in that same file.
- Keep one migration per change. Do not reset or squash unless the user asks.
- Seed permissions with role id `SUPERADMIN` or `ADMIN`. Role names are `SUPER ADMIN` and `ADMIN`.
- Do not print `DATABASE_URL` or `env.conf` secrets.
